-- Issue #912: CATALOG.SOURCE should contain a describe for every document type.
--
-- Before the fix it carried five: ENTITY, ENUMERATION, MICROFLOW, SNIPPET and
-- PAGE. Three more were already being collected by the catalog builder —
-- nanoflows, rules and workflows — but the executor's describe dispatch had no
-- case for rules and routed "nanoflow" to describeMicroflow, which searches
-- ListMicroflows() only and so returned NotFound for every nanoflow. The worker
-- loop discarded both errors, so those types produced zero rows in silence.
--
-- This script is a REPRO, not a check-time negative test: the defect lives in
-- the catalog builder, which needs a project, so `mxcli check` (which runs
-- without one) can only confirm the syntax. Run it against a project that has
-- nanoflows and mappings — a blank app with Atlas_Web_Content and
-- FeedbackModule is enough:
--
--   mxcli exec mdl-examples/bug-tests/912-catalog-source-all-doctypes.mdl -p app.mpr
--
-- Expected AFTER the fix: NANOFLOW, RULE, JSONSTRUCTURE, IMPORTMAPPING and
-- EXPORTMAPPING all appear below, and `refresh catalog source` reports no
-- "could not be described" lines.
--
-- Measured on a 9-module Mendix 11.6.6 project: 100 rows before, 118 after —
-- the 18 being 13 nanoflows, 1 rule, 2 JSON structures, 1 import mapping and
-- 1 export mapping. The unit guards are
-- TestDescribeDispatchCoversEverySourceObjectType (mdl/executor) and
-- TestRunDescribes_ReturnsFailuresInsteadOfSwallowingThem (mdl/catalog).

refresh catalog source;

-- Every document type that reached CATALOG.SOURCE. Before the fix this
-- returned exactly 5 rows; it now returns one per type the project contains.
select ObjectType, count(*) as Documents
from CATALOG.SOURCE
group by ObjectType
order by Documents desc;

-- The user-visible symptom. A nanoflow's body was not indexed, so searching for
-- anything only a nanoflow contains reported "No matches found" — while
-- helpfully suggesting `refresh catalog source`, which had already been run.
search 'DS_LoginContext';

-- Nanoflows specifically: zero rows before the fix, one per nanoflow after.
select QualifiedName, ModuleName
from CATALOG.SOURCE
where ObjectType = 'NANOFLOW'
order by QualifiedName;

-- The three types the report named. Each already had a catalog table and a
-- Reader method; only the source text was missing.
select ObjectType, QualifiedName
from CATALOG.SOURCE
where ObjectType in ('JSONSTRUCTURE', 'IMPORTMAPPING', 'EXPORTMAPPING')
order by ObjectType, QualifiedName;
